quran[9]{c,v,t}:
  3,92,"None of you shall ever attain righteousness until you spend out of what you love, and whatever thing you spend, Allah surely is All-Knowing of it."
  3,93,"All food was lawful to the Children of Israel except what Israel (Jacob) had forbidden himself before the Torah was revealed. Say: ‘Bring the Torah, and recite it if you are truthful.’"
  3,94,"So whoever fabricates lies about Allah after that, it is they who are the wrongdoers."
  3,95,"Say: ‘Allah has spoken the truth, so follow the religion of Ibrahim (Abraham), an upright man of pure faith, and he was not among the polytheists.’"
  3,96,"Indeed, the first House established for people (to worship Allah) is the one at Bakka (Mecca), a blessed sanctuary and a (centre of) guidance for all nations."
  3,97,"There are clear signs in it, (one of which is) the station of Ibrahim (Abraham). Whoever enters it shall be secure. Pilgrimage to this House is an obligation for Allah upon the people who can afford the journey to it. And whoever disbelieves, Allah is indeed beyond the need of (His) creatures."
  3,98,"Say: ‘O People of the Book! Why do you deny the revelations of Allah, while Allah is witness to what you do?’"
  3,99,"Say: ‘O People of the Book! Why do you bar the one who believes from the path of Allah, seeking to make it crooked, while you are witnesses (to its truthfulness)? And Allah is not negligent of what you do.’"
  3,100,"O believers! If you yield to a group of those given the Book, they will turn you back into disbelievers after you had believed."
